    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d699">

                <pb facs="0807" n="719" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg719"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McCormick to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-05-01"><hi rendition="#italic">May 1,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. McCormick reports that he has been advised that the viceroy replies that the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Hanyei Maru</hi> was seized at Miaodao because there
                    was evident proof of hostile intentions toward Russia; that the subjects on
                    board of the vessel were taken to Port Arthur and turned over to the judicial
                    authorities. Further particulars will be transmitted as soon as received.</p>
                <p>The viceroy has accepted the proposal for the exchange of information relating to
                    prisoners of war and will transmit such data as often as practicable, perhaps at
                    longer intervals than ten days, on account of local conditions.)</p>
            </div>
